cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "US-HealthBench: A Citation-Grounded, Multilingual Benchmark for Evaluating LLM Systems on Official U.S. Public-Health Guidance"
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "William Alston"
repository-code: "https://github.com/walston-health/us-healthbench"
url: "https://github.com/walston-health/us-healthbench"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-03-19"
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - public-health
  - LLM-evaluation
  - multilingual
  - health-informatics
  - citation-grounding
abstract: >-
  US-HealthBench is an open benchmark for evaluating large language models
  on consumer-facing public-health guidance from official U.S. sources
  (CDC, NIH, FDA, CMS). It includes English and Spanish tasks spanning
  factual retrieval, consumer action prompts, misinformation rebuttal,
  and cross-language consistency, scored on factual accuracy, citation
  support, safety, and multilingual reliability.
